# Retire policy 2026-11-20: still in production in 2026 with no announced end; retire dates commented out. Revisit when an end is announced.
# Toyota Prius XW60 five-door fastback plug-in hybrid, 2024 onwards.
#
# The fifth-generation Prius, sold in Britain as the plug-in hybrid only.
# Ordering opened on 4 March 2024 and the first customer cars arrived in
# July 2024; it was still on sale in the 2026 model year. Launch prices
# £37,315 Design and £39,955 Excel on the road.
# https://media.toyota.co.uk/toyota-announces-all-new-prius-plug-in-range-and-pricing/
# https://media.toyota.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/sites/5/pdf/Prius-prices-November-2026.pdf
#
# Dimensions 4.600 x 1.780 x 1.430 m, wheelbase 2.750 m. Source: English
# Wikipedia, "Toyota Prius" infobox, XW60 (model code XW60, production from
# December 2022): wheelbase 2,750 mm, length 4,600 mm, width 1,780 mm, height
# 1,420-1,430 mm. The hull measures 4.585 m long, 15 mm short of the published
# figure, 1.780 m wide, with the wheel centres 2.750 m apart. Mirrors take the
# modelled width to 2.064 m.
#
# Shape reference: the pack holds four three-quarter photographs and no side
# elevation, so the flank was built from them and from the published
# dimensions; a true elevation was rendered for the Gate B comparison but has
# no photograph to match. The reference cars are Japanese and American market
# cars; the British car is the plug-in hybrid, whose charging flap is not
# visible in any reference photograph and is therefore not modelled.
#
# Colours are Toyota GB names from the 2026 model year price list, evidence
# grade (a): solid Lunar Shadow; metallic Silver Metallic, Ash, Galaxy Black
# and Mustard; premium Platinum White Pearl and Scarlet Flare. Four are
# modelled: Silver Metallic, Ash, Galaxy Black and Scarlet Flare. Weights
# silver 3, ash 3, black 2, red 2, total 10, provisional pending the central
# rebase.
#
# Speed 175 km/h, just below the car's quoted 177 km/h because the plug-in
# hybrid's electric-only running does not govern its maximum. Comfort 120/510,
# on the line 330 + 1.5 x 120: the quietest and most refined of the Prius
# generations. Classes 1,2 only: the British plug-in model was priced well above
# the earlier cars, but a Toyota is not a plutocratic car and class 4 would put
# it in the hands of households that buy Rolls-Royces.
#
# Dates are road presence: July 2024 intro, retire dates commented out (still in production in 2026)
# twelve- to fifteen-year tail.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/toyota-prius-xw60.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/toyota-prius-xw60.dae (66 objects). References:
# citycars/references/toyota-prius-xw60/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: the nose is squarer than the photographs, the rear
# haunches are less pronounced and there are visible shading transitions at
# the wheel arches. The top view confirms a continuous painted roof between
# the windscreen and the hatch glass. At 128 px the low fastback roofline, the
# full-width rear lamp bar and the smooth flank read as the fifth-generation
# Prius.

obj=citycar
name=ToyotaPriusXW60(SilverMetallic)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=3
intro_year=2024
intro_month=7
#retire_year=2039
#retire_month=6
speed=175
length=3
class=1,2
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=120
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=510

Image[E]=./images/toyota-prius-xw60-silvermetallic_E.0.0,-33,14
Image[SE]=./images/toyota-prius-xw60-silvermetallic_SE.0.0,-13,0
Image[S]=./images/toyota-prius-xw60-silvermetallic_S.0.0,0,0
Image[SW]=./images/toyota-prius-xw60-silvermetallic_SW.0.0,-8,10
Image[W]=./images/toyota-prius-xw60-silvermetallic_W.0.0,4,5
Image[NW]=./images/toyota-prius-xw60-silvermetallic_NW.0.0,12,10
Image[N]=./images/toyota-prius-xw60-silvermetallic_N.0.0,0,33
Image[NE]=./images/toyota-prius-xw60-silvermetallic_NE.0.0,0,24
